 ### [Block Visibility Culling](5334-block-visibility-culling.md)
-Block Visibility Culling determines which voxel blocks require mesh updates or rendering based on the camera's position and rotation, avoiding unnecessary geometry generation when the view has not changed significantly. It operates at the coarse block level by comparing current camera coordinates and viewing direction against previous frame values, skipping index updates if both match. Unlike sibling methods that cull individual faces based on neighbor occupancy or surface orientation, this method optimizes the entire block's visibility state relative to camera movement.
